# Q2Translate repository contents
#
# The repository keeps only the inputs needed to build the portable
# application from a clean clone. Build output, the assembled package,
# screenshots, logs and the toolchain stay local.
#
# The assembled application is rebuilt by tools/deploy_portable.ps1 and is
# never committed.
#
# Build from a clean clone:
#   pwsh -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ./tools/download_toolchain.ps1
#   ./.toolchain/cmake/bin/cmake.exe -S . -B work -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
#   ./.toolchain/cmake/bin/cmake.exe --build work
#   pwsh -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ./tools/deploy_portable.ps1 -SkipBuild
#
# The release archives in build/ are intentionally not tracked: the full
# archive exceeds GitHub's 100 MB file limit. Publish both the full and the
# small archive as GitHub Release assets instead.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whitelist: ignore every top-level entry, then re-include the build inputs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/CMakeLists.txt
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/README_rus.md
!/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!/settings-default.json
!/src/
!/data/
!/docs/
!/resources/
!/third_party/
!/tools/
!/design/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly ignored local artifacts (kept for clarity and for tools that
# create them outside the whitelisted paths).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.toolchain/
/build/
/cmake-build-*/
/plugins/

# C++ / Qt generated files
*.o
*.obj
*.pch
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.idb
moc_*.cpp
moc_*.h
qrc_*.cpp
ui_*.h
*.moc
*.qmlc
*.jsc
*.pro.user
*.qmlproject.user

# IDE / OS files
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local logs and reports
*.log
tools/audit_*.txt
contrast_report.txt

# Local configuration
CMakeUserPresets.json
opencode.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
